== Notes ==
* {{t|Callus}} and {{i|Orphan Socks}} prevent Isaac from taking damage from spikes summoned by The Pile.
** {{t|Flat File}} has no effect on these spikes.

== Trivia ==
* The Pile originates from [https://www.reddit.com/r/bindingofisaac/comments/2tp3yi/boss_fight_mockup_the_pile/ a conceptual Reddit post] by NotYourSaggitarius on the Binding of Isaac subreddit in 2015. A few days later [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JmQHYbIEi-s it was programmed into Rebirth] by Kilburn, before being incorporated into the Antibirth mod.
** In Antibirth, The Pile could appear as a boss in the {{s|Mausoleum}}.
* It is a skeletal variant of {{e|Polycephalus}} and an even further decayed version of {{e|The Stain}}.
** This makes Polycephalus the only boss in the entire game to have more than one posthumous version.
* In its boss art, the rightmost head lacks 2 teeth on the bottom jaw, unlike its enemy sprite.
* The Pile is one of two bosses that can appear in both the main path and the alternate path, appearing in the {{s|Necropolis}} as well, the other being {{e|Reap Creep}}, who can appear in the {{s|Depths}} and {{s|Dank Depths}}.
** Because of this, its battle theme will be different, depending on where it's fought. If it's fought in Necropolis, either ''Crusade'' or ''Cerebrum Dispersio'' will play, while if it's fought in the Ashpit, ''Juggernaut'' will play.

